@startuml pipeline-status
title What is actually wired, and where the gap is

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF

rectangle "lib.rs::extractor\n#[proc_macro_derive(Extractor)]" as Entry #E8F4EA

rectangle "StructExtraction\n<&'ast DeriveInput>" as S #E8F4EA
rectangle "FieldExtraction\n<&'ast Field>" as F #E8F4EA
rectangle "TransformationExtraction\n<&'ast Attribute>" as T #FFD9D9
rectangle "SyntaxFieldAttributeExtraction\n<&'ast Attribute>" as Y #FFF4E5

rectangle "vocab suite\nflag! name_value! leaf!\nmeta_list! variants!\nnames! vocabulary!" as V #E8F4EA

rectangle "Processor" as P #EEEEEE
rectangle "Generator" as G #EEEEEE

Entry --> S : extract_from
S --> F : extract_each(data.fields.iter())
F --> T : extract_each(field.attrs.iter())

S ..> P : Extracted<..>, whole
P ..> G

V ..> P : the primitives it\nwill be written against
Y ..> V : uses SyntaxHelper\n(vocabulary!)

note bottom of T
  **todo!()** — would panic if reached.
  Nothing reaches it. Its job has changed:
  no longer a bespoke Meta matcher, but
  "read grammar type G from an opening",
  which is PROCESSOR work.
  (#attribute/generic-grammar)
end note

note bottom of Y
  Works and is tested, but driven ONLY by
  base/syntax/worked.rs — never by the macro
  path. The module carries an explicit
  ""#![allow(dead_code)]"" saying so, which comes
  off when the stages connect.
  (#syntax/not-driven)
end note

note bottom of V
  **Complete and green.** 78 tests. Reads a real
  attribute into a real value, every rejection
  case in SCRATCH.md's table covered.
  Depends on nothing downstream — which is why
  it could land before Processor exists.
end note

note bottom of P
  Comment-only stub in both crates.
  ""Extractor::Output"" is deliberately unbounded
  until this exists, because the honest bound
  is "whatever the processor can consume".
end note

legend right
  |<#E8F4EA>| live and tested |
  |<#FFF4E5>| works, tested, not wired |
  |<#FFD9D9>| todo!() — would panic |
  |<#EEEEEE>| does not exist yet |
endlegend

note as Gap
  **The load-bearing gap**

  The extraction tree is BUILT and then nobody
  reads it. ""StructExtraction.fields"" and
  ""FieldExtraction.transformation"" each carry
  an ""#[allow(dead_code)]"" naming this as the
  reason.

  lib.rs renders top-level reasons and emits a
  stub; the recursive walk is #syntax/render.
end note

Gap .. P

@enduml
